From 23b79ce0f240d9b16369936f35da3a574e41dc9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kevinbrar2024 <kevinbrar2024@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 06:21:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Finish a replacement's instructions before the player-loss
 check (CR 614.1c, CR 704.3)

A land's "as this land enters, choose a basic land type. Then you may pay
2 life" taken at exactly 2 life left its controller at 0 life with the
land-type choice still open. The terminal player-loss safety net ran
state-based actions inside that event; eliminating the player then tried to
abandon the resolution carrier with the post-replacement frame on top and
panicked. The net now waits while a replacement effect's own instructions
are the innermost unfinished work, as it already does for casts,
activations and mana abilities.

Co-Authored-By: Devin AI <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
